  1. Mailbox
  - The exact shared mailbox address, and confirmation it's a shared (or licensed) mailbox.

  2. Entra (Azure AD) app registration — a dedicated service principal for this integration, from which we'll need:
  - Tenant (Directory) ID
  - Application (Client) ID
  - Client secret or certificate (+ expiry date) 

  3. Graph API permissions (application type) + tenant admin consent
  - Mail.Read — if we only read messages, or
  - Mail.ReadWrite — if we should mark/move messages as "processed" after triage.
  

  4. Mailbox scoping (security)
  - An Application Access Policy restricting this app to only the shared mailbox above (so it can't access any other mailbox in the tenant).

  5. Environment / connectivity
  - Which Microsoft cloud (commercial graph.microsoft.com vs. a sovereign/GCC endpoint)?
  - Confirm our platform can reach login.microsoftonline.com and graph.microsoft.com — any proxy, firewall allow‑list, or
  Conditional Access exception we need to request?
